{:edb/db-before-t 2822 :edb/db-after-t 2823 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536135 50 #inst "2026-10-09T16:15:58.736Z" 13194139536135 true] [17592186096351 1100 "The area under the curve $y=4-x^2$ between $x=-1$, $x=2$, and the $x$-axis is approximated using a left Riemann sum, as shown below. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1042/Source/Images/ed16173ebe0275016a94e29e27948e67.png)" 13194139536135 false] [17592186096351 1100 "The area under the curve $y=4-x^2$ between $x=-1,$ $x=2,$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a left Riemann sum, as shown below. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079618/assets/b517da6e730ac50341b133a60ae8ab99cfed7b2ce92638e6028bb3fac6fbf9da.png)" 13194139536135 true] [17592186096351 1145 "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} f(x_k)\\Delta x\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx_k = a + k\\Delta x\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac{b-a}{n}\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=3$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=-1$ and $b=2$, so the step size is\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac{2-(-1)}{3} = \\dfrac 3 3 = 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(k = 0)^(n - 1)f(x_{k})Δx &= ∑_(k = 0)^(n - 1)f(a + kΔx)Δx \\\\\n&= ∑_(k = 0)^(3 - 1)f(-1 + k \\cdot 1) \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= ∑_(k = 0)^(2)f(k - 1) \\\\\n&= ∑_(k = 0)^(2)(4 - (k - 1)^{2}) \\\\\n&= ∑_(k = 0)^(2)(4 - k^{2} + 2k - 1) \\\\\n&= ∑_(k = 0)^(2)(3 + 2k - k^{2})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536135 false] [17592186096351 1145 "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} f(x_k)\\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwhere $x_k = a + k\\Delta x$ with $\\Delta x = \\dfrac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=3$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=-1$ and $b=2,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac{2-(-1)}{3} = \\dfrac 3 3 = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})Δx & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f(a+kΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{3-1}f(-1+k\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}f(k-1) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}(4-(k-1)^{2}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}(4-{k}^{2}+2k-1) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}(3+2k-{k}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536135 true] [17592186096352 1100 "The area under the curve $y=\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{ x}{2}\\right)$ between $x=0$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $3$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" 13194139536135 true] [17592186096352 1100 "The area under the curve $y=\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)$ between $x=0$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $3$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" 13194139536135 false] [17592186096352 1145 "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^n f(x_i)\\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwhere $x_i = a + i\\Delta x$ and $\\Delta x = \\dfrac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nNote that here we are using the index $i$ instead of $k.$ It doesn't matter which letter we use for the counter.\n\nWe're told that there are $n=3$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac{3-0}{3} = \\dfrac{3}{3} = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}f(0+i\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}f(i) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{i}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536135 true] [17592186096352 1145 "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{n} f(x_i)\\Delta x\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx_i = a + i\\Delta x\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac{b-a}{n}\n$$\n\nNote that here we are using the index $i$ instead of $k$. It doesn't matter which letter we use for the counter.\n\nWe're told that there are $n=3$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=3$. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac{3-0}{3} = \\dfrac{3}{3} = 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sum_{i=1}^{n} f(x_i)\\Delta x &= \\sum_{i=1}^{n} f(a + i\\Delta x)\\Delta x \\\\\n&= \\sum_{i=1}^{3} f(0 + i \\cdot 1) \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= \\sum_{i=1}^{3} f(i) \\\\\n&= \\sum_{i=1}^{3} \\cos\\left(\\frac{i}{2}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536135 false] [17592186096549 1020 #edb/ref 17592186385358 13194139536135 true] [17592186096549 1020 #edb/ref 17592186385361 13194139536135 true] [17592186096549 1020 #edb/ref 17592186385364 13194139536135 true] [17592186096550 1020 #edb/ref 17592186385369 13194139536135 true] [17592186096550 1020 #edb/ref 17592186385373 13194139536135 true] [17592186096550 1020 #edb/ref 17592186385376 13194139536135 true] [17592186096550 1020 #edb/ref 17592186385386 13194139536135 true] [17592186260055 1100 "The area under the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}(4x+8)$ between $x=-2$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a left Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $j$ and $n.$*\n\n${S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\frac{5}{n}\\,\\operatorname{sin}($\n{{field-1}}$)$" 13194139536135 false] [17592186260055 1100 "The area under the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x+8)$ between $x=-2$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a left Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $j$ and $n.$*\n\n${S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\frac{5}{n}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡($\n\n{{field-1}}$)$" 13194139536135 true] [17592186260055 1145 "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of subintervals, ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$, and  $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nThe endpoints indicate that $a=-2$ and $b=3,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-(-2)}{n}=\\frac{5}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(-2+j\\cdot \\frac{5}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\,\\frac{5}{n}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}(4(-2+\\frac{5j}{n})+8) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\,\\frac{5}{n}\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{20j}{n}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536135 false] [17592186260055 1145 "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of subintervals, ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$, and  $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nThe endpoints indicate that $a=-2$ and $b=3,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-(-2)}{n}=\\frac{5}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(-2+j\\cdot \\frac{5}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\,\\frac{5}{n}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(-2+\\frac{5j}{n})+8) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\,\\frac{5}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{20j}{n}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536135 true] [17592186260056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385368 13194139536135 true] [17592186261464 1017 #edb/ref 17592186274957 13194139536135 false] [17592186261464 1017 #edb/ref 17592186385380 13194139536135 true] [17592186261464 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/99f224712b0a067d76bc02c1f33938446ad84883a439ba53cb6569197e2cf9fd.png)\n\nThe area under the curve $y=\\frac{x+1}{x}$ between $x=1$, $x=4$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a left Riemann sum, as shown above. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" 13194139536135 false] [17592186261464 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079618/assets/99f224712b0a067d76bc02c1f33938446ad84883a439ba53cb6569197e2cf9fd.png)\n\nThe area under the curve $y=\\frac{x+1}{x}$ between $x=1$, $x=4$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a left Riemann sum, as shown above. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" 13194139536135 true] [17592186261487 1017 #edb/ref 17592186274964 13194139536135 false] [17592186261487 1017 #edb/ref 17592186385393 13194139536135 true] [17592186385358 1017 #edb/ref 17592186385359 13194139536135 true] [17592186385358 1089 "q-315701" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385358 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536135 true] [17592186385358 1100 "The area under the curve $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-4)$ between $x=2$ and $x=5$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a left Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $j$ and $n.$*\n\n${S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\frac{3}{n}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡($\n\n{{field-1}}$)$" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385358 1113 #uuid "18d22bab-9d00-5b28-aee4-2073bc2ebbb7" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385358 1145 "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of subintervals, ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$, and  $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nThe endpoints indicate that $a=2$ and $b=5,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{5-2}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(2+j\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\,\\frac{3}{n}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(2+\\frac{3j}{n})-4) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\,\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{6j}{n}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385359 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385360 13194139536135 true] [17592186385359 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536135 true] [17592186385359 1041 "field-1" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385359 1104 #edb/ref 17592186385360 13194139536135 true] [17592186385359 1110 #uuid "14892792-cc54-5740-9310-398085dbf81d" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385360 1034 "\\frac{6j}{n}" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385360 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536135 true] [17592186385360 1111 #uuid "d9c21429-afef-5da0-8202-11be6ddd791c" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385361 1017 #edb/ref 17592186385362 13194139536135 true] [17592186385361 1089 "q-315717" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385361 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536135 true] [17592186385361 1100 "The area under the curve $y=(x+2)^{3/2}$ between $x=-2$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a left Riemann sum using $10$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $j.$*\n\n${S}_{L}=\\frac{1}{2}$\n ${\\sum }_{j=0}^{9}($\n{{field-1}}$)^{3/2}$" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385361 1113 #uuid "2728f5cf-d423-5d6d-b117-9f0f9c4bc61a" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385361 1145 "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're given that there are  $n=10$ subintervals.  The endpoints indicate that $a=-2$ and $b=3,$  so the step size is \n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-(-2)}{10}=\\frac{5}{10}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{10-1}f(-2+j\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{9}f(\\frac{2j-4}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{9}{((-2+\\frac{j}{2})+2)}^{3/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{9}{(\\frac{j}{2})}^{3/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385362 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385363 13194139536135 true] [17592186385362 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536135 true] [17592186385362 1041 "field-1" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385362 1104 #edb/ref 17592186385363 13194139536135 true] [17592186385362 1110 #uuid "e55005cf-fd3c-5c5a-b364-407394b9b86a" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385363 1034 "\\frac{j}{2}" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385363 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536135 true] [17592186385363 1111 #uuid "54cbbc91-f971-50d1-bdfe-f67d7a062db3" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385364 1017 #edb/ref 17592186385365 13194139536135 true] [17592186385364 1089 "q-345027" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385364 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536135 true] [17592186385364 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079618/assets/e81e7d9d60e38c52f86c5eee784ebcfdeb91d4445b6539cc01a6ac9f5ededa89.png)\n\nThe area under the curve $y=\\frac{6}{x}$ between $x=1$, $x=6$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a left Riemann sum, as shown above. What is the expression for the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $k.$*\n\n${S}_{L}={\\sum }_{k=0}^{4}$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385364 1113 #uuid "fe864c7b-9ad1-5abf-a889-bb7b2a7a7382" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385364 1145 "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=5$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=1$ and $b=6,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{6-1}{5}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})Δx & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f(a+kΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{5-1}f(1+k\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{4}f(1+k) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{4}\\frac{6}{1+k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385365 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385366 13194139536135 true] [17592186385365 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385367 13194139536135 true] [17592186385365 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536135 true] [17592186385365 1041 "field-1" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385365 1104 #edb/ref 17592186385366 13194139536135 true] [17592186385365 1110 #uuid "8fc3d5df-590b-554b-9fad-df5140078067" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385366 1034 "\\frac{6}{1+k}" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385366 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536135 true] [17592186385366 1111 #uuid "dac1881b-9d38-5d55-b403-c105260f9981" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385367 1034 "\\frac{6}{2+k}" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385367 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536135 true] [17592186385367 1111 #uuid "76ce1408-4b6f-5f98-9970-8dbe17c284aa" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385368 1034 "\\frac{20j}{n}+8" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385368 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536135 true] [17592186385368 1111 #uuid "2f1d3e07-4c12-5426-91d7-f9501aa9d9c0" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385369 1017 #edb/ref 17592186385370 13194139536135 true] [17592186385369 1089 "q-345037" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385369 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536135 true] [17592186385369 1100 "The area under the curve $y=\\sqrt{4x+8}$ between $x=-2$ and $x=2$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $8$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $i.$*\n\n${S}_{R}=\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385369 1113 #uuid "0cebe607-010c-5dd8-9460-ab5f20c202b1" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385369 1145 "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is   \n\n$$\n{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n=8$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=-2$ and $b=2.$ So, the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{2-(-2)}{8}=\\frac{4}{8}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(-2+i\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}f(-2+\\frac{i}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}\\,\\sqrt{4\\,(-2+\\frac{i}{2})+8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}\\,\\sqrt{2i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385371 13194139536135 true] [17592186385370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385372 13194139536135 true] [17592186385370 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536135 true] [17592186385370 1041 "field-1" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385370 1104 #edb/ref 17592186385371 13194139536135 true] [17592186385370 1110 #uuid "5370c979-ad27-551a-9c6e-df209e21e5f3" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385371 1034 "\\sqrt{2i}" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385371 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536135 true] [17592186385371 1111 #uuid "e8d147c3-255f-563d-8366-a9c38946ae51" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385372 1034 "\\sqrt{2i+8}" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385372 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536135 true] [17592186385372 1111 #uuid "4bbbf0a4-a602-5069-b4c7-0868f3a3a06f" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385373 1017 #edb/ref 17592186385374 13194139536135 true] [17592186385373 1089 "q-345048" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385373 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536135 true] [17592186385373 1100 "The area under the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x-3)$ between $x=1$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $j$ and $n.$*\n\n${S}_{R}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\frac{2}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡($\n{{field-1}} $)$" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385373 1113 #uuid "d783f47f-8c35-5b8a-93f4-00f2091ffca3" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385373 1145 "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=1$ and $b=3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-1}{n}=\\frac{2}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[f(1+j\\cdot \\frac{2}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{2}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(1+\\frac{2j}{n})-3)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\frac{2}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1+\\frac{8j}{n}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385374 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385375 13194139536135 true] [17592186385374 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536135 true] [17592186385374 1041 "field-1" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385374 1104 #edb/ref 17592186385375 13194139536135 true] [17592186385374 1110 #uuid "cecd0e6b-5c07-58e7-88f6-555151104bec" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385375 1034 "\\frac{8j}{n}+1" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385375 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536135 true] [17592186385375 1111 #uuid "908d759e-a0ba-5899-b1ce-c908c48106f1" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385376 1017 #edb/ref 17592186385377 13194139536135 true] [17592186385376 1089 "q-345052" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385376 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536135 true] [17592186385376 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079618/assets/f321b063e3bc76eeb5b426d00cbf94451a06cec928008eaadc965547691c412a.png)\n\nThe area under the curve $y=4+x$ between $x=0,$ $x=4$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a right Riemann sum, as shown above. What is the expression for the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $i.$*\n\n${S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}($\n{{field-1}} $)$" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385376 1113 #uuid "e378236a-5e54-5371-98f4-4839b4a8b16f" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385376 1145 "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=4$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=4,$ so the step size is \n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-0}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(0+i\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(i) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}(4+i).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536135 true] [17592186385377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385378 13194139536135 true] [17592186385377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385379 13194139536135 true] [17592186385377 1040 #edb/re